<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rota</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">words <a href="/years/1908">1908</a>, first published 7 November <a href="/years/1908">1908</a>; music <a href="/years/1910">1910</a>, first sung 15 July <a href="/years/1910">1910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Konopnicka, a poet and activist for Polish independence, wrote &quot;Rota&quot; (&quot;The Oath&quot;) in 1908 while staying in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Cieszyn</a>, as a protest against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>'s policy of forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanisation">Germanisation</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> in the lands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> had annexed in the partitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>.</p></div>
